 were  lying on the concrete floor holding  their wounds and allowing themselves to  quietly bleed to death their faces aglow  with a strange in her light christmas  and isaac and a few remaining followers  still on the side of the living had been  backed into a far corner their faces  white and terrified as they saw the  growing numbers of the Church of the  Dead it was clearly going to be no  contest  Kirsten finally managed to squeeze off a  few pictures before cramming the camera  back into her bag and heading for the  exit no one had noticed her so far and  Booker no books she wasn't going to let  this continue any longer she would have  to get out to call the police or someone  who could come in here and stop all of  this whatever it was that was happening  in the guttering dimness she saw shapes  gathering ahead of her blocking her way  to the exit panicked she crouched down  and ran straight out them hoping to  force her way through by keeping her  body as far from their searching teeth  as possible the space near the door was  nearly all shadows and she shoved her  way ahead blindly lashing out with her  arms in her heavy equipment bag for a  moment she couldn't breathe feeling as  though the smell of the candles and the  blood was choking her and she tried to  scream but no sound came out just when  she thought she could see the door ahead  nothing more than a rectangular crack of  light floating in a black space she felt  hands clawing at her from all sides  fingers scraping across her back and  shoulders she did scream then but her  scream was lost him and the agonized  howling from Christus and his few  holdouts who had finally fallen to the  adherents of the new creed in the  stinking darkness Kirsten felt her bag  and her clothes being ripped away and  before the fingers and teeth began to  sink into her flesh she had time to  think of her forced conversion time to  think of whether she would remember  herself when she awakened as an acolyte  of this 